{"title":"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If two dice are tossed, the probability that the product of the numbers showing on the tops of the dice is greater than 10 is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6159bb302a98d91ebdc1ce4eabdfbdc18445cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{17}{36}\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{11}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"371\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there are no possibilities for the second dice.\n</p><p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the second dice can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, giving one possibility.\n</p><p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the second dice can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810bc0baedbccc52fc6a497d568ec41502f9dc27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,5,6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, giving three possibilities.\n</p><p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the second dice can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3523fb5c4052f272f059b452b5fc133f4b287012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,4,5,6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, giving four possibilities.\n</p><p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the second dice can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3523fb5c4052f272f059b452b5fc133f4b287012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,4,5,6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, giving four possibilities.\n</p><p>When the first dice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the second dice can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/264eaaa8b6cffaf3d6ec10f6d9b61d55bedd8538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3,4,5,6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, giving five possibilities.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>The total number of ways for the product to greater than 10 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a84c8737442464ee18b78b38d97b13a442a135f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+4+4+5=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" /> and the total number of possibilities is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7309b641c29c9d16cbb6ba3221f99e555b6a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)(6)=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, yielding a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/cedd9fff8f4c8e344cd759a05dab32cda141b0c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{17}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"64\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME\" title=\"1992 AJHSME\">1992 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1992 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1992 AJH